      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Blocking issues must be resolved before approval.\n\n### Review Summary\n- **Functionality**: ❌ Moving the ODR validation before `k_mutex_lock(s-\u003emutex, K_FOREVER)` and `lis2dh_enable_fifo(s, LIS2DH_FIFO_BYPASS_MODE)` fixes the mutex leak and FIFO bypass issue on rejected rates, and pre-checking `rate \u003c 0 || rate \u003e LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL` avoids signed shift overflow in `LIS2DH_ODR_TO_REG()`. However, `LIS2DH_ODR_TO_NORMALIZE()` clamps any rate `\u003c\u003d 1000` up to `1000` (`LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL`), so positive rates below `LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL` with `rnd \u003d\u003d 0` (e.g., `rate \u003d 500, rnd \u003d 0`) silently round up to `1000` mHz instead of failing with `EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM`.\n- **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit**: ✅ Pre-validating ODR parameters before acquiring the sensor mutex and reconfiguring the hardware FIFO matches the ChromiumOS EC motion sensor driver contract (`EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM` on invalid rates without mutating hardware state).\n- **Code Simplicity**: ⚠️ Adding `rate \u003e LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL` at line 291 makes the post-normalization bounds check (`normalized_rate \u003e LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL || normalized_rate \u003c LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL`) on lines 303–305 completely unreachable. In addition, initializing `normalized_rate \u003d 0` and `reg_val \u003d LIS2DH_ODR_0HZ_VAL` on lines 287–289 is redundant as long as lines 328–336 retain a separate `if (rate \u003d\u003d 0)` branch that hardcodes `LIS2DH_ODR_0HZ_VAL` and `0`.\n- **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability**: ✅ Follows Zephyr/ChromiumOS EC C conventions and error-return idioms.\n- **Security**: ✅ Preventing signed shift overflow in `1 \u003c\u003c (31 - __builtin_clz(_odr / 25000))` for large `rate` values and preventing permanent mutex lockup on invalid input hardens the host-command/sensor path against out-of-range parameters.\n- **Testing**: ❌ `test_lis2dh__set_data_rate` only tests `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL * 2` and `-1`, missing exact boundary values (`LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL`, `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL + 1`, `INT_MAX`, and `LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL`), the `rnd \u003d\u003d 0` rounding-down path when `normalized_rate \u003c rate`, and verification that the FIFO remains enabled when an invalid rate is rejected under `ACCEL_LIS2DH_INT_ENABLE`.\n- **CL Size \u0026 Scope**: ✅ Small, focused bug fix (+33, -14 lines across 2 files).\n- **Commit Message**: ⚠️ Clearly states the motivation, `BUG\u003d`, and `TEST\u003d` lines, though the body narrates internal macro/variable names and omits mentioning that negative rates are now rejected rather than clamped to 1 Hz.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/a1a4e189-07cd-4c38-8653-eb5563cb57ac)",
