      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Checking `rate \u003e LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL` on line 291 makes the post-normalization bounds check on lines 303–305 unreachable, while still allowing positive rates below `LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL` (`1000` mHz) to succeed when `rnd \u003d\u003d 0`:\n\n1. **`normalized_rate \u003c LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL` is always false:** `LIS2DH_ODR_TO_NORMALIZE(_odr)` returns `1000` (`LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL`) for all `_odr \u003c\u003d 1000`, and `LIS2DH_REG_TO_NORMALIZE(reg_val)` returns at least `LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL` for all `reg_val \u003e\u003d LIS2DH_ODR_1HZ_VAL`. Consequently, calling `set_data_rate(s, 500, 0)` (requesting a rate below 1 Hz without rounding up) silently rounds **up** to `1000` mHz instead of returning `EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM`.\n2. **`normalized_rate \u003e LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL` is always false:** `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL` (`MOTION_MAX_SENSOR_FREQUENCY(400000, 25000)`) is an exact supported step (`25000 \u003c\u003c k`). When `rate \u003d\u003d LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL`, `normalized_rate \u003d\u003d rate` so `rnd \u0026\u0026 (normalized_rate \u003c rate)` is false; when `0 \u003c rate \u003c LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL`, `normalized_rate` before rounding is at most the step immediately below `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL`, so `reg_val++` yields at most `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL`.\n\nReject sub-minimum rates when `!rnd` in the upfront guard and remove the unreachable post-normalization check:\n\n```c\n\tif (rate \u003c 0 || rate \u003e LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL ||\n\t    (!rnd \u0026\u0026 rate \u003e 0 \u0026\u0026 rate \u003c LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL))\n\t\treturn EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM;\n\n\tif (rate \u003e 0) {\n\t\treg_val \u003d LIS2DH_ODR_TO_REG(rate);\n\t\tnormalized_rate \u003d LIS2DH_ODR_TO_NORMALIZE(rate);\n\n\t\tif (rnd \u0026\u0026 (normalized_rate \u003c rate)) {\n\t\t\treg_val++;\n\t\t\tnormalized_rate \u003d LIS2DH_REG_TO_NORMALIZE(reg_val);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/a1a4e189-07cd-4c38-8653-eb5563cb57ac)",
