      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Expand the boundary and branch coverage for `set_data_rate()` so off-by-one mutations, shift-overflow inputs, rounding modes, and FIFO state preservation are verified:\n\n1. **Upper boundary (`LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL`, `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL + 1`, and `INT_MAX`):** Testing only `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL * 2` does not catch mutating `rate \u003e LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL` to `rate \u003e\u003d LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL`, nor does it exercise large positive values (`INT_MAX`) that previously caused signed shift overflow in `LIS2DH_ODR_TO_REG()`. Verify that `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL` succeeds and sets `drvdata-\u003ebase.odr \u003d LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL`, while `LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL + 1` and `INT_MAX` return `EC_RES_INVALID_PARAM`.\n2. **Rounding-down branch (`rnd \u003d\u003d 0`) and lower boundary (`LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL`):** All valid rate assertions currently pass `rnd \u003d 1`, leaving `if (rnd \u0026\u0026 (normalized_rate \u003c rate))` untested when `rnd \u003d\u003d 0` and `normalized_rate \u003c rate` (e.g., `set_data_rate(acc, 15000, 0)` rounding down to `10000`, and `set_data_rate(acc, LIS2DH_ODR_MIN_VAL - 1, 0)` vs. `rnd \u003d 1`).\n3. **FIFO mode and state preservation on rejected rates:** Because `test_common.c` is also compiled into the `drivers.lis2dh.interrupt` suite (`ACCEL_LIS2DH_INT_ENABLE`), assert that rejected rates (both `\u003e LIS2DH_ODR_MAX_VAL` and `\u003c 0`) leave `acc-\u003emutex-\u003elock_count \u003d\u003d 0`, `drvdata-\u003ebase.odr` unchanged, and the FIFO enabled (`if (IS_ENABLED(ACCEL_LIS2DH_INT_ENABLE)) zassert_true(lis2dh_emul_is_fifo_enabled(emul));`).\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/a1a4e189-07cd-4c38-8653-eb5563cb57ac)",
